Checkpoint 5 validation runbook - Windy image acquisition
==========================================================

Checkpoint outcome
------------------

Checkpoint 5 retrieves due active Windy streams, compares the current
`lastUpdatedOn` marker with stored state, skips unchanged images, downloads and
fully decodes changed `preview` images, and updates ingestion state only at the
correct stage. It does not transform images, use S3, or publish MQTT messages.

1. Confirm branch and protected configuration
---------------------------------------------

    cd /home/codexuser/src/webcam-iot-ingest
    git branch --show-current
    git status --short
    git diff --check
    git check-ignore -v .env .secrets/windy_api_key .secrets/database_password

The branch must be `codex`. Do not print secrets or discard unrelated changes.

2. Verify PostgreSQL
--------------------

    docker compose --env-file .env up -d postgres
    docker compose exec postgres pg_isready
    uv run --env-file .env python -m database.healthcheck

Do not delete or recreate the PostgreSQL volume.

3. Run the focused automated checks
-----------------------------------

    uv run --env-file .env pytest tests/ingestion tests/test_deployment_config.py -q
    RUN_DATABASE_TESTS=1 uv run --env-file .env pytest tests/database/test_registry_queries.py -q
    uv run --env-file .env python -m ingestion.windy.windy_ingestion_workflow --help

These checks cover marker equality, rendition selection, bounded streaming,
complete decoding, invalid and oversized bodies, throttling/retry behaviour,
country selection, due-state filtering, and database state transitions.

4. Run bounded memory-only samples
----------------------------------

    uv run --env-file .env python -m ingestion.windy.windy_ingestion_workflow --countries DK --limit 3 --dry-run
    uv run --env-file .env python -m ingestion.windy.windy_ingestion_workflow --countries DK,MT --limit 4 --dry-run

The JSON output must contain names, countries, dimensions, formats, and outcome
counts, but no tokenized image URLs or credentials. `--dry-run` must not change
markers, timestamps, or EMA values. When several countries are requested, the
limit is divided between them; a country with fewer due streams may leave some
of the global limit unused.

5. Validate the real freshness transition on a tiny sample
----------------------------------------------------------

Run one applied camera, then repeat the same command:

    uv run --env-file .env python -m ingestion.windy.windy_ingestion_workflow --countries DK --limit 1
    uv run --env-file .env python -m ingestion.windy.windy_ingestion_workflow --countries DK --limit 1

Inspect the affected state:

    docker compose exec postgres psql -U webcam_ingestion -d webcam_ingestion -c \
      "SELECT source_stream_id, last_provider_image_marker, last_download_timestamp, ema_download_period FROM source_stream ss JOIN site s USING (site_id) WHERE s.network_id = 'win' AND s.country = 'DK' ORDER BY last_download_timestamp DESC NULLS LAST LIMIT 5;"

The first successful changed image records its marker, UTC timestamp, and EMA.
If the same stream is selected and its Windy marker has not changed, its outcome
is `unchanged` and its image body is not downloaded. The minimum interval can
make another never-downloaded due stream sort first; the automated test is the
deterministic assertion of the exact same-stream unchanged case.

